[[The final hold|warrior_queen_day_2_13]]


:: warrior_queen_day_2_13

Sixty consecutive seconds. That was the goal.

I had managed thirty. Forty. Forty-five. Each attempt ended in a tremor that began in the calves, climbed through the thighs, entered the core, and shook the entire structure until the stance collapsed like a tower with its keystone removed.

The sixty-second attempt began at — I guessed — mid-afternoon. The sun had burned through the mist and was now baking the Iron Garden into a stone oven. My leathers were dark with sweat. The binding was thoroughly saturated. The sand sack was somehow even heavier when wet, the sand absorbing moisture and adding weight that Nyssa's careful adjustment could not account for.

