Sixty seconds.

I held for sixty seconds without a wobble.

Aldric, who had been watching with a timepiece I had not known he possessed — produced from a pocket with the casual revelation of a man who owned exactly one sentimental object — looked at the dial. Looked at me.

And gave the nod.

The nod.

I unlocked my stance. My legs buckled immediately — I caught myself on the weapons rack, both hands gripping the wood, head hanging, sweat dripping from my nose and chin and the tips of my long hair. The sand sack hung from my chest like a penance. Beneath it, the breasts pulsed with a relieved, almost //grateful// ache, as though the tissue itself was glad the ordeal was over.

<<speech "aldric">>Tomorrow. Dawn. Bring nothing.<</speech>>

He turned and walked away. Frostfang silent at his hip. Footsteps receding. Stone and silence.

I hung from the weapons rack and breathed. Belly-breathing. The way he had taught me.

In the centre of my body, in the place where the new strength was being forged, something that was not quite muscle and not quite will and not quite hope — but was perhaps all three — burned steadily.

[[Return to chambers — evening|warrior_queen_day_2_14]]


