[[Sleep — Day 2 ends|warrior_queen_day_2_21]]


:: warrior_queen_day_2_21

I ate the soup. It was good. Halda's work — rich, savoury, thick with root vegetables and a warmth that felt like being held.

I applied the salve again myself, before bed. Maera was right — the more I touched them, the less strange they felt. My own fingers on my own breast skin. The circular motions. The areola's sharpened sensitivity. The nipple's deep, radiating pulse. These were //my// sensations, produced by //my// body, and every night I practiced them was a night I became less of a stranger in my own flesh.

