They were there. They were growing. They were becoming a permanent part of me, alongside the hips and the waist and the hair and the voice and the face that was softening in the mirror. And today, in the Iron Garden, standing in the feminine guard with a sand sack on my chest and a warrior's breath in my belly, I had felt something I had not expected to feel.

I had felt the //potential//.

Not the body I had lost. Not the prince who was dissolving. But the thing //growing// beneath the dissolution — the fighter in the feminine guard, the warrior whose strength lived in the centre, the queen whose body would carry breasts and blades and a crown and the weight of an entire kingdom.

Not there yet. Not close. But the foundation was laid.

